(771, 9, 100, 1, 1, '2025-04-27', 'Fox in the bowl', 'Kettu kulhoon', 1, 0, 'The episode title is a reference to the ‘See no fox, hear no fox, speak no fox’ task.', 'In this season premiere, the contestants must bring in something they would like to throw into the middle of the Nevada desert, get a fox into a bowl, draw the most consecutive red cards from a deck, make the most magnificent donkey bridge, and end up with the most bananas. The guest contestant is VilleGalle.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '|667|', '|667|', NULL, NULL, 'suurmestari_06_01_framed.png', 'suurmestari_06_01_metatag.jpg', 'suurmestari_06_01_thumb.jpg', 'Image of VilleGalle, the guest contestant on the episode.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(772, 9, 100, 2, 1, '2025-05-04', 'Change the room in the dark', 'Muuta huonetta pimeässä', 1, 0, 'The episode title is a reference to the ‘Transform the lab while the lights are out’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the best thing to use for measuring that isn’t a real measure, transform the lab while the lights are out, choose a word and get someone to repeat it as much as possible during a phone call, destroy something as spectacularly as possible, and avoid saying Jaakko’s favourite thing. The guest contestant is Juuso Kallio (aka Köpi).', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '|668|', '|668|', NULL, NULL, 'suurmestari_06_02_framed.png', 'suurmestari_06_02_metatag.jpg', 'suurmestari_06_02_thumb.jpg', 'Image of Juuso Kallio (aka Köpi), the guest contestant on the episode.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(773, 9, 100, 3, 1, '2025-05-11', 'Sort the chocolates correctly', 'Lajittele suklaat oikein', 1, 0, 'The episode title is a reference to the ‘Sort the chocolates and dance’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the best ugly object, save eggs from a blender, correctly sort coloured chocolates while dancing, gift-wrap themselves in the most surprising way, and create an animal on the back of a T-shirt they are wearing. The guest contestant is Lina Schiffer.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '|664|', '|664|', NULL, NULL, 'suurmestari_06_03_framed.png', 'suurmestari_06_03_metatag.jpg', 'suurmestari_06_03_thumb.jpg', 'Image of Lina Schiffer, the guest contestant on the episode.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(774, 9, 100, 4, 1, '2025-05-18', 'Find the squirrel', 'Etsi orava', 1, 0, 'The episode title is a reference to the ‘Find the squirrel’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the most surprising thing that starts with an ‘F’, find a squirrel on a football pitch, build a tower of cans in the lab, be as disappointing as possible, and mislead Jaakko about the contents of a briefcase. The guest contestant is Linnea Leino.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '|665|', '|665|', NULL, NULL, 'suurmestari_06_04_framed.png', 'suurmestari_06_04_metatag.jpg', 'suurmestari_06_04_thumb.jpg', 'Image of Linnea Leino, the guest contestant on the episode.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(775, 9, 100, 5, 1, '2025-06-01', 'Fairy Godmother', 'Hyvä haltiatar', 1, 0, 'The episode title is a reference to the ‘List your wishes, then make them come true’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the most jaw-dropping item, list wishes (and then make them come true), ring a bell, daringly put an egg into an eggcup, and deliver an impromptu speech. The guest contestant is Karoliina Tuominen.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '|666|674|', '|666|674|', NULL, NULL, 'suurmestari_06_05_framed.png', 'suurmestari_06_05_metatag.jpg', 'suurmestari_06_05_thumb.jpg', 'Image of Karoliina Tuominen, the guest contestant on the episode.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(776, 9, 100, 6, 1, '2025-06-08', 'Medium-sized circle', 'Keskikokoisin ympyrä', 1, 0, 'The episode title is a reference to the ‘Draw the median medium-sized circle’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the most surprising thing that fits through a letter box, divert sand from one bucket to another, draw the median medium-sized circle, complete the most tasks, and survive a game of ‘Jaakko Says...’. The guest contestant is Lakko.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '|528|', '|528|', NULL, NULL, 'suurmestari_06_06_framed.png', 'suurmestari_06_06_metatag.jpg', 'suurmestari_06_06_thumb.jpg', 'Image of Lakko, the guest contestant on the episode.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(777, 9, 100, 7, 1, '2025-06-15', 'Synchronised presentation', 'Tahdistettu esittely', 1, 0, 'The episode title is presumably a reference to either the ‘Create as many new identities as possible’ or ‘Make the bookcases identical’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the most fox-like thing that is not a fox, create as many new identities as possible, give the most Suurmestari-like person the most impressive high-five possible, make two bookcases identical, and make a member of the audience look like Pilvi. The guest contestant is Cristal Snow.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '|666|', '|666|', NULL, NULL, 'suurmestari_06_07_framed.png', 'suurmestari_06_07_metatag.jpg', 'suurmestari_06_07_thumb.jpg', 'Image of Cristal Snow, the guest contestant on the episode.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(778, 9, 100, 8, 1, '2025-06-22', 'Find a mandarin', 'Etsi mandariini', 1, 0, 'The episode title is simply a reference to the ‘Find the mandarin in a sock’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in something they once regretted buying but no longer do, find a mandarin hidden in a line of identical socks, perform the greatest deed possible with their little finger, and catch balls in a stovepipe hat. The guest contestant is Jarkko Niemi, but he is represented in the studio by season 5 guest contestant <a href=\"/person.php?id=536\">Sointu Borg</a> (the two met and became good friends while <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.is.fi/menaiset/ihmiset-ja-suhteet/art-2000009946775.html\">competing on the same season of the Finnish version of <em>Dancing with the Stars</em> in 2023</a>).', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '|528|', '|528|', NULL, NULL, 'suurmestari_06_08_framed.png', 'suurmestari_06_08_metatag.jpg', 'suurmestari_06_08_thumb.jpg', 'Image of Sointu Borg, the guest contestant in the studio for this episode, representing Jarkko Niemi.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(779, 9, 100, 9, 1, '2025-06-29', 'Pick something up and carry it far away', 'Nosta jotain ja vie kauaksi', 1, 0, 'The episode title is a reference to the ‘Transport something you can lift as far as possible’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the most confusing thing from their wardrobe, put a sock in a box (or a box in a sock), lift something above their shoulders and then move it as far away as possible, achieve the greatest outcome with a single breath, and name musical acts in alphabetical order. The guest contestant is Oona Kare.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '|666|', '|666|', NULL, NULL, 'suurmestari_06_09_framed.png', 'suurmestari_06_09_metatag.jpg', 'suurmestari_06_09_thumb.jpg', 'Image of Oona Kare, the guest contestant on the episode.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(780, 9, 100, 10, 1, '2025-07-06', 'Crazy mocktail', 'Mieletön mocktail', 1, 0, 'The episode title is a reference to the ‘Make and serve Pilvi a dramatic mocktail’ task.', 'In this season finale, the contestants must bring in the best thing to be awarded as a prize on Suurmestari, put the most stuff on top of a jelly, predict what a contestant will do with an object before doing something themselves, make and serve Pilvi a dramatic mocktail, and duel the opposing team in a series of challenges set by Jaakko. The guest contestant is Katja Ståhl.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '|673|', '|673|', NULL, 'The final episode scoreboard shows Hissu, Iina and Sonja each with one less point than they were actually awarded.|The cause of this discrepancy is unknown, but it seems possible that they were accidentally awarded 2 points each for the ‘Make and serve Pilvi a dramatic mocktail’ task, rather than the 3 points each that Jaakko announced.|This error did not affect the contestants’ placings in the episode, or for the season overall.', 'suurmestari_06_10_framed.png', 'suurmestari_06_10_metatag.jpg', 'suurmestari_06_10_thumb.jpg', 'Image of Katja Ståhl, the guest contestant on the episode.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(781, 1, 76, 1, 1, '2025-05-01', 'Sometimes spit', NULL, 1, 32, 'Alex Horne claims that he has been known to “Sometimes spit”, when asked by Jason Mantzoukas what cool things he does, during the ‘Do something really cool backwards’ task.', 'In this series premiere, the contestants must bring in the object that most reminds them of school (in a good way), pour all of their vinegar into a fish tank, do something really cool backwards, win the Pealympics, and get the most raisins into their wine glass.', NULL, 'Hello, thank you. I’m Greg Davies. Welcome to this brand-new series of Taskmaster. I have never felt so full of hope. The tasks are new, the contestants are new. And whilst I was enjoying my single origin espresso this morning, they were being shaved down and put through our 12-point hygiene programme, ready for battle. So they all smell just great... for now. So let’s meet the new recruits, ready to risk it all to take home daddy’s golden head… ‘Daddy’s golden head of destiny’ is a sentence I forgot I wrote.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And next to me, a man who is a lifelong supporter of Liverpool Football Club, and tells me that the only downside to that is meeting the other fans, who he finds to be universally stupid and physically disgusting. It’s little Alex Horne!', NULL, NULL, NULL, '|599|', '|599|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_uk_19_01_framed.png', 'taskmaster_uk_19_01_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_uk_19_01_thumb.jpg', 'Photo of a some garden peas frozen in an arrangement resembling the Olympic rings (referencing the \'Win the Pealympics task\'), with the episode title, \'Sometimes spit\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(782, 1, 76, 2, 1, '2025-05-08', 'An invisible jump rope', NULL, 1, 598, 'Jason Mantzoukas suggests that everyone “Imagine there’s an invisible jump rope in there”, before footage of Stevie Martin’s strange jumping gait during the ‘Give Alex 100 marbles on a plate, and an egg cup full of tepid water’ task is replayed yet again on the screen, in the studio.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the snootiest thing, achieve a really tricky thing after first commentating on the achievement, give Alex 100 marbles on a plate and an egg cup full of tepid water, get the most liquid into a can without leaving the submari-van, and put one item completely inside another.', NULL, 'Hello and welcome to Taskmaster! I’m Greg Davies and I suit things. I suit this throne. I suit this suit. I suit the title of Taskmaster, and I suit the power it affords me. What can I say? I suit things. I suit boots. I suit fruits. I suit flutes and, once, I was in cahoots with some mute newts about a car boot in Bute. Proof, if it was needed, that the writing of these introductions is becoming increasingly challenging. No matter, let’s take the focus off me, and train the glaring judgmental super trooper into the frightened eyes of some human bunnies.\r\n', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And next to me, a man whose hobbies include bird-spotting, writing songs, and his absolute favourite: having extramarital affairs. It’s Little Alex Horne!', NULL, NULL, NULL, '|599|', '|599|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_uk_19_02_framed.png', 'taskmaster_uk_19_02_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_uk_19_02_thumb.jpg', 'Photo of ice containing coloured balls, frozen in the shape of a rubber duck, perched on top of a microphone on an oil drum in the driveway of the Taskmaster house (referencing the \'Get the most liquid in this can\' and \'Achieve a really tricky thing after commentating on the achievement\' tasks), with the episode title, \'An invisible jump rope\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(783, 1, 76, 3, 1, '2025-05-15', 'My presumably scrotum', NULL, 1, 599, 'Mathew Baynton states that “It was not my intention to upstage Stevie with my, presumably, scrotum” after watching his own attempt at the ‘Answer the cheese phone’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the best thing for a middle-aged man to keep on his bedside table, answer the cheese phone, move the most cushions from one bin to the other, paint a picture of the Taskmaster and his assistant having fun, and obey Greg’s previous orders.', NULL, 'Hello! Hello, I\'m Greg Davies. Welcome to Taskmaster. There\'s a famous Shakespearian idiom which simply states ‘Brevity is the soul of wit’. Well, I\'m taking advice from you, am I? A man who wear a giant detachable collar? Doubt it. I\'ve heard you didn\'t even write your plays, Shakey, swear down. Give me advice about what\'s funny? Running around London with a big codpiece sticking out of your leggings, and I\'m listening to you about the introduction to a comedy show, am I? Wouldn\'t have thought so, Shakespeare. What should I do, just come on and say ‘Forsooth’ or something? That\'s proper put me in a bad mood that has. Going bald and then growing your hair long anyway. Now you\'re lecturing me about introductions? That\'s proper put me in a bad mood that has, Shakey. So... good luck to our contestants.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And next to me, a man who told me in private that he once ran his fingers over the seat of a chair because someone told him Princess Anne had sat on it. It\'s little Alex Horne!', NULL, 'So what have we learnt today? We\'ve learnt so many things in this episode. So many things have happened. And yet, every single person watching this show tonight will remember just one thing: this. Of course here he is, your winner once more, Mathew Baynton.', 'Greg is, of course, referring to the image of Mathew inadvertently exposing himself to the world as he crawls along the hallway of the house in his too-short shorts during the ‘Answer the cheese phone’ task.', '|599|', '|599|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_uk_19_03_framed.png', 'taskmaster_uk_19_03_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_uk_19_03_thumb.jpg', 'Photo of some cheese and a rainbow of poster paint on an artist\'s palette in the garden of the Taskmaster house (referencing the \'Answer the cheese phone\' and \'Paint a picture of the Taskmaster and his assistant having fun\' tasks), with the episode title, \'My presumably scrotum\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(784, 1, 76, 4, 1, '2025-05-22', 'Midnight picnic', NULL, 1, 19, 'Greg Davies sarcastically says “I’m so sorry to interrupt the children’s midnight picnic”, when Jason Mantzoukas and Stevie Martin decide to sit on the stage floor to confer over their guesses to the ‘Bluff the other team’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the thing that least suits its name, put the most wetsuits on mannequins, bluff the other team, tell Alex why the light bulb turns on, and win a game of Front-ham.', NULL, 'Hello, I am Greg Davies. Welcome, once more, to Taskmaster. We all know the score: five trophy-hungry comedians rip open some medieval envelopes, and then run around having a breakdown, which I mark out of five. I’m a dreamer, and one day  those cowards at Channel 4 will take my Squid Games crossover proposal seriously. But for now, regrettably, it’s only their careers that are in danger.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And next to me, a man who wrote under a pseudonym to his local paper, saying that he thinks disabled access regulations in shops are ‘political correctness gone mad’. In the Chesham Gazette, he’s Dr Stephen Morris, but we know him as little Alex Horne.', NULL, NULL, NULL, '|600|', '|600|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_uk_19_04_framed.png', 'taskmaster_uk_19_04_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_uk_19_04_thumb.jpg', 'Photo of a circular yellow token with an expressionless face on it, leant against a red light bulb on a small wooden box (referencing the \'Tell Alex why the light bulb turns on\' task), surrounded by a large hourglass, a golden pineapple, and a rubber duck, with the episode title, \'Midnight picnic\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(785, 1, 76, 5, 1, '2025-05-29', 'Maybe we\'re the monsters', NULL, 1, 19, 'Greg Davies suggests that “Maybe we\'re the monsters!” during his end of episode sign-off, referencing Rosie Ramsey’s mistaken belief that the contestants were meant to draw themselves during the ‘Draw the monster’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the best object to bequeath to a relative against whom they are seeking revenge, be the least annoying person around the campfire, draw a monster while sitting in a car, write down every word they’d said before opening the task, and pop a balloon when they hear its colour. Also, two contestants face off in a tiebreaker to punch the most holes in a sheet of paper.', NULL, 'Hello, thank you. Welcome, one and all, to Taskmaster. One of the many TV shows that my own nieces don’t watch, and yet am I expected to display your school photos in my home? I doubt it! They’ve gone in the drawer, with years’ worth of your rubbish artwork. I know you’ll never hear this, but it’s enough for me to know that I’ve said it on TV. Quid pro quo, you monsters! Quid pro quo!', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And next to me, a man who drives an electric car, and to quote him, ‘Not for the good of the planet, but because it makes my wife horny.’ It’s little Alex Horne!', NULL, 'So what have we learnt today? Well, I guess we’ve learnt that people always try their best to be nice, to be considerate to others. But sometimes, when we put humans under extreme pressure, they reveal things that they don’t want anyone to know about themselves. Maybe we’re the monsters! Half done, half to go, but for now it’s all about Jason Mantzoukas!', NULL, '|598|', '|598|', 'Jason wins the episode after beating Rosie in the tie-breaker.', NULL, 'taskmaster_19_05_framed.png', 'taskmaster_19_05_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_19_05_thumb.jpg', 'Photo of a two pencils (one long, one short) in a double pencil sharpener, with a flame coming out of the end, seen in the wing mirror of a car (referencing the \'Draw the monster\' and \'Write down every word you said before opening the task\' tasks), with the episode title, \'Maybe we\'re the monsters\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(786, 1, 76, 6, 1, '2025-06-05', 'It\'s got to be obsolete', NULL, 1, 598, 'Jason Mantzoukas says “Oh, whatever it is, it’s got to be obsolete.” while mocking Alex Horne’s choice to study Latin and Greek at Cambridge University, during the ‘Teach Alex a lesson he’ll never forget’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the thing that is nicest to open, work out what Alex has on top of his head, capture a classic family home video moment, teach Alex a lesson he’ll never forget, and not be the one to blow the last thing off the table.', NULL, 'I’m Greg Davies, and welcome to Taskmaster. It’s episode six, and, unlike any of the meals my mother served me throughout my childhood, things are really hotting up. They’ve proved themselves to be resilient, clever, and, unlike any of the food fed to me up until the age of 18, they have just the right amount of spice. Even some salt would’ve helped, for god’s sake, old woman. Put some salt in! It tastes of nothing!', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And next to me, a man who told me privately that for him, sex is like Christmas: once a year, and involves the death of a turkey. It’s little Alex Horne!', NULL, NULL, NULL, '|597|', '|597|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_uk_19_06_framed.png', 'taskmaster_uk_19_06_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_uk_19_06_thumb.jpg', 'Photo of the reflection of someone\'s eye in the end of a periscope, in front of the Taskmaster house (referencing the \'Work out what Alex has on top of his head\' task), with the episode title, \'It\'s got to be obsolete\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(787, 1, 76, 7, 1, '2025-06-12', 'Glass half most', NULL, 1, 600, 'Rosie Ramsey says “Glass half most” whilst choosing between writing the word ‘most’ or ‘least’ during the ‘Eat the yoghurt with the most/least dignity’ task, presumably trying to convey that she’s making her choice because she’s an optimist.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the biggest anti-climax, find out what’s in a yellow box, eat some yoghurt with the most or least dignity, put at least six litres of water in a vase, and get one of their balls into their bucket.', NULL, 'Hello, everybody! I’m Greg Davies. Welcome to Taskmaster. So far, the competition has seen the steely determination of British Blitz spirit, and whilst I must be respectful and not do too many wartime analogies when discussing a light entertainment show, there are some similarities. We’ve seen resilience, determination, steadfast strength in the face of adversity and, crucially, a brash American sweep in and try and take all the glory. Let’s hope he leaves without getting loads of our women pregnant after buying them nylons. Let’s get on and begin the next round of the competition and meet our mighty five once more.', 'During the Second World War, nylon was prioritised for use in military applications, so it was difficult for women in the UK to get hold of new nylon stockings. When American soldiers came to the UK, they brought nylon stockings with them to help gain the affections of British women.', NULL, NULL, 'And next to me, a man who told me that when you’re a busy father, work-life balance can be tricky, but he’s developed a  technique on the nights that he’s in charge of the kids. And I quote him, ‘I stick them in front of an iPad and I spark up a fat one.’ Little Alex Horne!', NULL, NULL, NULL, '|599|', '|599|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_uk_19_07_framed.png', 'taskmaster_uk_19_07_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_uk_19_07_thumb.jpg', 'Photo of a small yellow wooden cube floating in a large vase full of water (referencing the \'Find out what’s in the yellow box\' and \'Put at least six litres of water in the vase\' tasks), with the episode title, \'Glass half most\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(788, 1, 76, 8, 1, '2025-06-19', 'Science all your life', NULL, 1, 599, 'Mathew Baynton sings “science all your life” as part of his improvised theme tune to the ‘Science Today’ show, during the ‘Obey the autocue’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the best object that you’ve borrowed from a fairly close friend, fail a task in the most heartbreakingly spectacular way, paint a memorable scene to convey three words, obey an autocue, and guess whether the next person will have a higher or lower number of things than the previous person.', 'During his introductory banter section, Alex shows a QR code to the camera, which links to an <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://bingo.taskmaster.tv/\">interactive bingo card</a> of exact and slightly inexact quotes from the episode.', 'Hello, welcome to Taskmaster, or as they call it in Wales... [WELSH ACCENT:] Alright, boys, how’s it going? Oh, it’s cold at the moment, innit? Oh, I’ll have to wear my big coat. Fair play. It is cold, mind, innit? Eh, do you know my brother? He looks like my brother, he does. The competition is really hurtling towards a conclusion, so please welcome the warriors holding on for dear life.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And next to me, a man who says that women should be like the landmark Shard building in London - they should look attractive, remain silent and have a glass ceiling firmly in place. Don’t shoot the messenger. Shoot little Alex Horne!', NULL, NULL, NULL, '|601|', '|601|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_uk_19_08_framed.png', 'taskmaster_uk_19_08_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_uk_19_08_thumb.jpg', 'Photo of some paints and paintbrushes inside a washing machine (referencing the \'Paint a memorable scene to convey three words\' task), with the episode title, \'Science all your life\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(789, 1, 76, 9, 1, '2025-06-26', 'Getaway sticks', NULL, 1, 598, 'Jason Mantzoukas refers to Alex Horne’s legs as “getaway sticks” at the start of the ‘Create new bodies and become a dynamic duo with Alex’ task.\r\n\r\n', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the most satisfying thing you could use as a jelly mould, place something somewhere surprising, create new bodies and become a dynamic duo with Alex, give Patatas the elixir, and play a game of word chess.', NULL, 'Hello! Welcome, welcome to Taskmaster. I\'m Greg Davies, and for a man my age, I\'m as fly as they come. We\'re at the penultimate stage of a competition that will go down in history as being so unimportant that I doubt any of us that are involved will even have marked graves. That said, we\'re here now, so let\'s make an effort.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And next to me, a man that went to private school and genuinely doesn\'t like people knowing that. It\'s Little Alex Horne!', NULL, 'It\'s the final next, but for now there\'s just one winner, and it\'s Jason Mantzoukas!', NULL, '|598|', '|598|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_19_09_framed.png', 'taskmaster_19_09_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_19_09_thumb.jpg', 'Photo of several task briefs attached to both the windvane on top of the Taskmaster house, and an action figure straddling one of the windvane\'s arms (referencing the \'Place something somewhere surprising\', \'Create new bodies and become a dynamic duo with Alex\' and \'Give Patatas the elixir\' tasks), with the episode title, \'Getaway sticks\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(790, 1, 76, 10, 1, '2025-07-03', 'The clever side?', NULL, 1, 598, 'After Greg Davies describes Jason Mantzoukas’s stalling tactic during the ‘Provide the best drive-through experience’ task as “So clever”, and Alex Horne claims that they’ve “not seen that side of you before, Jason”, Jason asks him “The clever side?”.', 'In this season finale, the contestants must bring in the thing most likely to make you do a double-take, completely fill a yellow box with sand, freeze in a powerful pose for 10 minutes, provide the best drive-through experience, and get the most carrot into their buckets.', NULL, 'Hello! Welcome to the Taskmaster grand final! Ten weeks of literal blood, sweat and tears, and we are a short hour away from crowning not just any clown, the king of the clowns! What makes a champion, ladies and gentlemen? Blood? We’ve seen it. Sweat? All five of our  contestants stink of it. Tears? Every night, when he wets the bed. So, we all have the  ingredients for one final pie - the glory pie. Please meet the meat that hopes to end up being its filling.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And next to me, a man who tells me the secret to a happy marriage is simple: respect; making time for your personal space; and never telling your wife, Rachel, how boring all her stories are. It’s little Alex Horne!', NULL, NULL, NULL, '|601|', '|601|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_uk_19_10_framed.png', 'taskmaster_uk_19_10_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_uk_19_10_thumb.jpg', 'Photo of a some ice cubes, some sand, and a baseball cap featuring an image of some french fries in a metal bucket (referencing the \'Completely fill the yellow box with sand\' and \'Provide the best drive-through experience\' tasks), with the episode title, \'The clever side?\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(791, 8, 111, 1, 1, '2025-08-18', 'It’s like a Make A Wish', NULL, 1, 698, 'Alice Snedden states “Wow, this is like a Make-A-Wish”, in response to Jack Ansett’s accidental success during the ‘Get the balloon through the hole and into the jar’ task.', 'In this season premiere, the contestants must bring in the thing that gives them the most street-cred, bounce a ball off of as many walls as possible before felling a toilet roll tower with it, film an origin story for their favourite idiom, get a balloon through a hole and into a jar without touching it, and throw fish into a barrel.', NULL, 'Tena koutou katoa. Nau mai, haere ma, and welcome to a brand-new Taskmaster New Zealand. My name is Jeremy Wells, and every year, as part of my charity work in the Big Buddy, Little Buddy programme, I arrange for five comedians to spend\ntime with my little buddy Paul here, completing a series of tasks that feel surprisingly high-stakes, considering the fact that none of this matters in the slightest.  These comedians aren\'t just hereout of the goodness of their hearts; they\'re here for this ― my golden head. So, let\'s introduce the five comedians who, for the next 10 weeks, will be gaining points and losing dignity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And joining me, as always, is the man who calls me his best friend for life and who I\'m proud to call an occasional colleague. It\'s my assistant, ladies and gentlemen, Paul Williams.', NULL, 'We are already 10% through the series, but what have we learned from episode one? Well, we learned that Alice Snedden\nis one better than Barack Obama; if you can\'t find a ball, then we haven\'t hidden it; and most importantly, we\'ve learned that the winner of episode one is Alice Snedden. Ma te wa. We\'ll see you next time.', NULL, '|698|', '|698|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_nz_06_01_framed.png', 'taskmaster_nz_06_01_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_nz_06_01_thumb.jpg', 'Image of a small New Zealand flag planted in the top of a fabric mountain peak in the lab (a reference to Bree Tomasel\'s attempt at the \'Film an origin story for your favourite idiom\' task), with the episode title, \'It’s like a Make A Wish\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(792, 8, 111, 2, 1, '2025-08-19', 'Toxic Sexual Energy', NULL, 1, 698, 'Alice Snedden states that “there was a real sort of toxic sexual energy” in the room when she and Bree Tomasel were secretly trying to out-alpha one another, during the ‘Draw a portrait of the Taskmaster playing ping-pong’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the thing that is way heavier than it looks, draw a portrait of the Taskmaster playing ping-pong (during which some team members have to also attempt to out-alpha the rest of their team), find a cake and eat it, attempt to re-enact the other team’s first meeting, and display as many emotions as possible in four seconds.', NULL, 'Kia ora koutou, and welcome to Taskmaster. Tonight, five comedians will compete in a series of tasks that are as frustrating as they are trivial all in pursuit of this ― a beautiful golden trophy that previous winners have discovered is massively undervalued at Cash Converters.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And to my left is a man who is saved in my phone as ‘Leggy Brunette ― Work’. It\'s Paul Williams.', NULL, 'Tonight we\'ve learned, you\'re either born an alpha or you\'ve bribed someone with Lego; and there\'s nothing more devastating than looking for cake. But most importantly, we\'ve learned that the winner of episode two is Jackie van Beek!', NULL, '|701|', '|701|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_nz_06_02_framed.png', 'taskmaster_nz_06_02_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_nz_06_02_thumb.jpg', 'Image of a small stack of books on a bookshelves, the topmost of which has been covered in icing (a reference to the \'Find your cake and eat it\' task), with the episode title, \'Toxic Sexual Energy\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(793, 8, 111, 3, 1, '2025-08-25', 'Get out of my Box', NULL, 1, 700, 'Jack Ansett insists that Bree Tomasel “Get out of my box” in the early stages of the ‘Make the tallest free-standing structure’, after the two contestants interfere with one another’s progress.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the non-feline thing with the most feline energy, drop an egg on a target from a rollercoaster, recreate an uncomfortable teenage moment with a different outcome, collect the most coins, and make the tallest free-standing structure.', NULL, 'Nau mai piki mai, and welcome to Taskmaster. My name is Jeremy Wells, and six years ago, while on a high school field trip, I was bitten by a radioactive and judgemental spider, who was particularly good at reading autocue. Since then, I\'ve had no choice but to wield the great responsibility of being a friendly neighbourhood Taskmaster. And joining me on my hero\'s journey are four New Zealand comedians, and also one Australian, who lied on the forms and tricked her way in.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And to my left in a lower chair and a lower tax bracket, it\'s my loyal assistant, Paul Williams.', NULL, 'Ka kite ano. We\'ll see you next time.', NULL, '|698|', '|698|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_nz_06_03_framed.png', 'taskmaster_nz_06_03_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_nz_06_03_thumb.jpg', 'Image of a rubber duck on the corner of the table in the lab, which has compost scattered across it (a reference to Jack Ansett\'s attempt at the \'Collect the most coins\' task), with the episode title, \'Get out of my Box\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(794, 8, 111, 4, 1, '2025-08-26', 'Who knows who I am?', NULL, 1, 700, 'Jack Ansett asks the audience “By round of applause, who knows who I am?”, after Jeremy rules that Pax Assadi has more of a career to lose, while awarding points during the ‘The thing that will be your downfall’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the thing that will be their downfall, bust out of prison, film an extremely climatic scene, complete seven tasks in 40 seconds, and make the most unique noise.', NULL, 'Kia ora koutou, and welcome to Taskmaster ― the show that comedians say ‘yes’ to because they\'re desperate to reinvent themselves, or, in Jack Ansett\'s case, invent themselves. My name\'s Jeremy Wells, and I am the Taskmaster. Tonight, our five comedians will be competing in a series of wickedly complex tasks. And for their efforts, they can win this ― a beautiful rendition of my bonce ― the creation of which broke at least three of the Ten Commandments. And I would like to once again apologise to my neighbour\'s oxen.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And beside me, as always, is a man who would do anything for me. And I would do some things for him, provided I haven\'t got anything else on. Ladies and gentlemen, it\'s Paul Williams!', NULL, 'So, what have we learned this week? We\'ve learned the difference between a climax and a cliff-hanger. And we\'ve learned that when you\'re breaking out of prison, less people is more. But most importantly, we\'ve learned that the winner of this episode is Bree Tomasel!', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'In the final task, Jeremy awards Alice 1 point, but her score increases by 2 points.', 'taskmaster_nz_06_04_framed.png', 'taskmaster_nz_06_04_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_nz_06_04_thumb.jpg', 'Image of a skeleton lying on the grass, being overlooked by a fibreglass zebra dressed as a St Bernard (a reference to Jackie van Beek\'s attempt at the \'Film an extremely climatic scene\' task), with the episode title, \'Who knows who I am?\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(795, 8, 111, 5, 1, '2025-09-01', 'Two guys on a mop', NULL, 1, 67, 'Jeremy Wells asks Pax Assadi “what was gonna be mind-blowing about two guys on a mop?”, during studio discussion of his attempt at the ‘Take the most mind-blowing photo’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the two best things that rhyme, take the most mind-blowing photo, kick a ball into the caravan, improve New Zealand’s national anthem, get a ball into a clown’s mouth, and count the popcorn popped.', NULL, 'Nau mai piki mai, and welcome to Taskmaster. May name is Jeremy Wells, and if you’re watching this on demand, please feel free to skip ahead six seconds to when this introduction is over and we finally get to the good bit when I tell you that I am the Taskmaster. With me on stage tonight are five winners of life and losers of tasks.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And next to me, as always, because every principal first violinist needs someone by their side playing second fiddle, it’s the one, the only Paul Williams!', NULL, 'Po manahau, Aotearoa.', NULL, '|699|', '|699|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_nz_06_05_framed.png', 'taskmaster_nz_06_05_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_nz_06_05_thumb.jpg', 'Image of the lower half of a wooden zebra statue with balls of yarn in various colours hanging from it, on the floor of the lab (a reference to Jackie van Beek\'s attempt at the \'Take the most mind-blowing photo\' task), with the episode title, \'Two guys on a mop\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(796, 8, 111, 6, 1, '2025-09-02', 'A Duck Archery Fanatic', NULL, 1, 701, 'Jackie van Beek says to Jeremy Wells that “I\'m getting a vibe that you might be a cricket fanatic, and not so much a kind of duck archery fanatic”, during studio discussion of her and Alice Snedden’s attempts at the ‘Demonstrate exceptional aim’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the best thing to snap, deliver a burger to the caravan while completing mini-tasks, demonstrate exceptional aim, quickly get the gist of the book <em>The Scarlet Pimpernel</em> and then adapt it for the screen, and recount a boring story that Paul told them during their time at the house.', NULL, 'Welcome to Taskmaster. My name is Jeremy Wells, and earlier this year, in a secret conclave, I was selected to be the leader of the Roman Catholic Church. However, I traded that position in to become something far more powerful, and now I am the Taskmaster. Joining me tonight are my faithful cardinals...', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And by my side, as always, is a man who lives his life in the fast lane except at the Glenfield Leisure Centre swimming pool, where he was asked to move to the slow lane. It’s Paul Williams!', NULL, 'See you next time. Ma te wa.', NULL, '|698|', '|698|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_nz_06_06_framed.png', 'taskmaster_nz_06_06_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_nz_06_06_thumb.jpg', 'Image of a purple plastic ball inside a small orange plastic cone, lying on a lawn (a reference to Pax Assadi\'s attempt at the \'Demonstrate exceptional aim\' task), with the episode title, \'A Duck Archery Fanatic\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(797, 8, 111, 7, 1, '2025-09-08', 'Community Hip-Hop', NULL, 1, 701, 'Jackie van Beek states that “I do community hip-hop every Tuesday” while defending her attempt at the ‘Get the ball in the hole’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the best thing to take on a road trip, get a ball in the hole on a rotating platform, dazzle a pair of senior citizens, knock over a domino in the lab, and unbox a box before delivering its contents to a sandbox.', NULL, 'Kia ora koutou katoa, and welcome to Taskmaster. My name\'s Jeremy Wells. Join me in welcoming my five favourite comedians of the season.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And beside me, a man who\'s asked me to adopt him so many times I\'ve lost count, an act that his real dad calls ‘hurtful and generally upsetting’.', NULL, 'Another episode filled with incredible lessons. We\'ve learnt that Jackie van Beek is an adult hip-hopper, and no-one\'s crotch is safe around Pax and a golf club. And most importantly, we\'ve learnt that Jackie van Beek is the winner of episode seven.', NULL, '|701|', '|701|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_nz_06_07_framed.png', 'taskmaster_nz_06_07_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_nz_06_07_thumb.jpg', 'Image taken from the bottom of a golf hole, looking up at a flag against the sky (a reference to the \'Get the ball in the hole\' task), with the episode title, \'Community Hip-Hop\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(798, 8, 111, 8, 1, '2025-09-09', 'Hoisted on a Petard', NULL, 1, 702, 'Pax Assadi tells Alice Snedden that “You are definitely not hoisted on a petard”, during studio discussion of the ‘Score 43 points playing the duck toss’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must: bring in the best present for Paul; create new numbers, score 43 points playing the duck toss; perform a party trick; build a toilet paper tower in the middle of a trampoline; and burst a balloon, crack a can of soda, pop a champagne cork, or bang a confetti cannon.', NULL, 'Tena koutou katoa. Welcome to Taskmaster, the show where five comedians are given a living wage, and in exchange, at least three times a year for the rest of their lives, they will wake up in a cold sweat, remembering how they couldn’t find a camera that was made of cake. My name is Jeremy Wells, and I am the Taskmaster.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And as always, sitting next to me, a man who doesn’t like sparkling water because he thinks it’s too spicy: it’s Paul Williams.', NULL, 'Thanks, everyone. We’ll see you next time. Po marie.', NULL, '|700|', '|700|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_nz_06_08_framed.png', 'taskmaster_nz_06_08_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_nz_06_08_thumb.jpg', 'Image of several toilet rolls scattered on a lawn in front of the legs of a trampoline (a reference to the \'Build a toilet paper tower in the middle of a trampoline\' task), with the episode title, \'Hoisted on a Petard\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(799, 8, 111, 9, 1, '2025-09-15', 'Comfortable in your own skin', NULL, 1, 701, 'Jackie van Beek tells Jack Ansett that “I don’t think you’re comfortable in your own skin”, during studio discussion of the ‘Get a former contestant to say a specific phrase’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the thing that looks the most like them, find plastic bears hidden in some items by picking the right one, write and perform a one-minute scene for a musical about Sherlock Holmes, get a former contestant to say a specific phrase, and fan a ping pong ball around a race track.', NULL, 'Nau mai, haere mai. Welcome to Taskmaster. My name’s Jeremy Wells, and I am descended from a man named Giuseppe Wells, who invented the idea of giving things points. He raised a family of point-givers, who eventually produced me,\r\nthe greatest point-giver of them all. And thus, I was chosen to be the Taskmaster. We are just one episode away from finding out which of our five comedians will win this ― a bust of my head, made with asbestos and painted gold with 80% lead-free paint. But first, we have to find out who will win episode nine, so let’s get things started by introducing the comedians fighting for glory ― or at least minimum embarrassment.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And, as always, to my left, he’s the EA who’s just OK ― it’s Paul Williams!', NULL, 'One more episode down and only one more to go. But what have we learnt? Well, we’ve learnt never to rely on David Correos. And we learnt &#127925; Job, job, job, job, job, job, job &#127925;. But most importantly, we learnt that Jackie van Beek is the winner of episode nine!', NULL, '|701|', '|701|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_nz_06_09_framed.png', 'taskmaster_nz_06_09_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_nz_06_09_thumb.jpg', 'Image of a sparkly gold hat and a small plastic toy bear lying on the lawn in front of some plinths (a reference to the \'Pick the right one\' task), with the episode title, \'Comfortable in your own skin\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(800, 8, 111, 10, 1, '2025-09-16', 'Seen as sneaky', NULL, 1, 701, 'Jackie van Beek asks whether it would be “seen as ‘sneaky’” if she were to watch the other contestants making their planes, during the ‘Make paper aeroplanes and fly them the furthest’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the best thing that rhymes with ‘information’, protect a pig from a wolf, grab a leaf, bump Paul’s boat, and make paper aeroplanes and fly them the furthest.', 'Throughout the studio portions of this episode, all of the contestants are wearing wigs, just as Jackie van Beek had been doing in the studio during each of the previous episodes.|At the start of the episode, Taskmaster AU’s assistant Tom Cashman makes a cameo appearance as Paul William’s stunt double, performing a running forward roll on the stage.|The title of this episode originally listed in the TV schedule was ‘Locked and loaded’. Based on the <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/taskmaster/comments/1nia0gl/comment/nemfyeb/\">account</a> of an individual who attended the filming of the episode, there were originally recurring references in the episode to Jack Ansett resembling a school shooter. These were presumably edited out of the episode at the last minute due to news relating to one or more recent shooting incidents, meaning that the episode title also had to be changed.', 'Nau mai, haere mai, and welcome to the most important event in the televisual calendar: the series finale of Taskmaster. My name is Jeremy Wells, and once again, we find ourselves marvelling at these five deeply weird human beings. Over the past nine episodes, we’ve seen them fall and rise, but mostly fall. Soon it will be all over, and you can once again go on Reddit and complain about how I score things. Just let me say, I don’t care, and I never will, because I am the Taskmaster. And tonight we’ll find out which of our five comedians will go home with this ― the golden Taskmaster trophy. The other four will leave with nothing but memories that they’ll never forget, no matter how hard they try.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'By my side, a man who will gorge himself on nuts, berries, and salmon right after we finish this episode, and then go into hibernation until we start filming series seven. It’s Paul Williams!', NULL, 'The moment of truth. It’s time to announce the winner of season six. And what a season it’s been. We’ve had climaxes and clowns. We’ve had hidden Pauls, hidden cakes, and balls that weren’t hidden – they just rolled away. And it’s all led to this.', NULL, '|700|', '|700|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_nz_06_10_framed.png', 'taskmaster_nz_06_10_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_nz_06_10_thumb.jpg', 'Image of some pieces of broken egg shell and panels made up up glued-together lollipop sticks lying on a concrete floor (a reference to the \'Protect the pig\' task), with the episode title, \'Seen as sneaky\', superimposed on it.', 'taskmaster_nz_06_10_2_adj.jpg', 'Image of Taskmaster AU’s assistant Tom Cashman making his cameo appearance as Paul William’s stunt double, running back across the stage in front of the contestants, who are all wearing wigs.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
