(834, 1, 77, 1, 1, '2025-09-11', '9 x 7', NULL, 1, 32, 'Alex Horne says “Nine times seven” during scoring of the ‘Do something that sounds disgusting but is actually really nice’ task.', 'In this series premiere, the contestants must bring in a very soft thing which would be most beneficial for Greg Davies, honk a horn, roll an object onto a target, do something that sounds disgusting but which is actually really nice, and try to end up on their spot while obeying Greg’s instructions.', NULL, 'Hello! Thank you. Welcome to Taskmaster, a set of challenges presided over by a temperamental dictator. It’s a sort of upbeat North Korea, and I’m Kim Jong-Fun.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And next to me, a man who I once thought I saw riding on the back of a baby elephant with a tiny trunk, to discover he simply had no trousers on. It’s… little Alex Horne!', NULL, NULL, NULL, '|693|', '|693|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_uk_20_01_framed.png', 'taskmaster_uk_20_01_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_uk_20_01_thumb.jpg', 'Photo of an ice ball with a letter \'Q\' embedded within it, and a wooden tile with the letter \'R\' printed on it, lying in front of a target consisting of concentric blue, white and red rings (referencing the \'Honk the horn\' and \'Roll an object onto the target\' tasks), with the episode title, \'9 x 7\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(835, 1, 77, 2, 1, '2025-09-18', 'Cows are made of milk', NULL, 1, 692, 'Ania Magliano suggests that “cows are made of milk” during studio discussion of her attempt at the ‘Identify Alex’s five things with one sense’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the object that is hardest to describe, identify Alex’s five things with one sense, remove the most flour from a tray using their superpowers, take the most surprising thing out of a bag, and guess how many things Alex has on him.', 'The final episode scoreboard features photos of the contestants’ ducks from the ‘Remove the most flour from the tray using your superpowers’ task, in place of their usual portraits.', 'Hello. Thank you, thank you. Welcome to Taskmaster, the great leveller. Comedians come with their plaudits and their impressive careers and achievements, and soon realise that, in this arena, they’re just people, simply humans taking on life’s challenges. Which throws up the question I get asked in the street all the time: ‘Will we, the members of the public, ever get to be on the show?’. No, not on my watch. Why? I simply don’t want you on it. Ever. Leave it! Line drawn. Let’s move on. Let’s meet the people who deserve to be here.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And next to me, a lover, a fighter, a bit of a biter. He’s got a wonky tooth and his hair’s got much whiter... it’s little Alex Horne.', NULL, NULL, NULL, '|695|', '|695|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_uk_20_02_framed.png', 'taskmaster_uk_20_02_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_uk_20_02_thumb.jpg', 'Photo looking up at a task brief attached to a small pink umbrella, hanging from the foliage of a flowering laburnum tree (referencing the \'Take the most surprising thing out of this bag\' task), with the episode title, \'Cows are made of milk\', superimposed on it.', 'taskmaster_uk_20_02_2.jpg', 'Image of the final scoreboard, which features photos of the contestants’ ducks from the ‘Remove the most flour from the tray using your superpowers’ task, in place of their usual portraits.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(836, 1, 77, 3, 1, '2025-09-25', 'Thompson', NULL, 1, 692, 'Ania Magliano asks the woman in the lab if their name is “Thompson”, during the ‘Discover the name of the person in the lab’ task, based on the fact that the name is written on their sweatshirt.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the thing they were least likely to bring in from home, make a little model of the Chesham United mascot, discover the name of a person in the lab, win a game of ‘Snakes & Steps’, and turn a cup triangle upside-down.', NULL, 'Hello, welcome. Welcome to Taskmaster. I’m Greg Davies, a juicy fillet steak of manhood, if I do say so myself. Take the heat off – I’m rare and I’m ready for the plate. Who dares to sit at the table of white-hot competition and complete tasks to make me sizzle on my judgmental skillet? Who dares to face my pepper-scorn sauce? Who wants my champion chips enough to risk getting their just deserts? Let’s find out. Here they are!', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And next to me, a man who told me that on a childhood visit to a fruit farm, he once sneakily ate so many strawberries that he achieved the holy grail – the unbroken three-foot stool. It’s little Alex Horne! ', NULL, 'What have we learned today? Well, I believe we’ve learnt the very definition of victory. Is it the person with the most points? No. Is it the person who heads home with the prizes? No. The definition of victory is getting a fellow competitor to take home a vial of your own piss. We’ll see you next time, but for now here’s the episode winner, Maisie Adam! ', NULL, '|693|', '|693|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_uk_20_03_framed.png', 'taskmaster_uk_20_03_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_uk_20_03_thumb.jpg', 'Photo of a green plastic toy snake and two chess pieces on a chess board, and their reflections in a mirror (referencing the \'Make a little model of the Chesham United mascot\', \'Discover the name of the person in the lab\', and \'Win a game of Snakes & Steps\' tasks), with the episode title, \'Thompson\', superimposed across the squares of the bottom row of the chessboard (and also reflected in the mirror).', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(837, 1, 77, 4, 1, '2025-10-02', 'Hey mate', NULL, 1, 694, 'Phil Ellis wastes valuable time during his 10-second voice message to Sanjeev Bhaskar during the ‘Make a love heart with your team’ task by starting with the phrase “Hey mate”.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the most gorgeous birthday gift ever, find out what number Alex has written down with only 20 questions, make a love heart with their team-mates, win a horse race by doing things involving olives and grapes, and deceive the Taskmaster about what they’ve written on their form. In a thrilling tie-breaker, two contestants then have to remove their shower caps by inflating a balloon.', NULL, 'Yes, hello! Welcome to Taskmaster, the show that is as meaningful as an old man sweeping up autumnal leaves only to have them blown across the garden overnight. And yet, five people want to take part. Why? Ego? A competitive streak? Well, according to a chat I just had in the green room with one of the competitors, it\'s no more complicated than an unhappy home life. Let\'s play on and welcome them.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And next to me, a man who once told me that there isn\'t a single presenter in the ITV daytime schedule that he hasn\'t thought about when having solo fun time... it\'s little Alex Horne!', NULL, 'So, what have we learnt today? Well, we\'ve learnt that, no matter what happens, no matter who it ha– [PHONE RINGS] So sorry… Hello? Yeah, yeah. Phwoar. Phwoar, yeah. Yeah. Oh, defo. Absolutely, yeah. Later, though. I\'m at work. I told you. You can\'t ring me at work. Whoa! Alex\'s mum. But, more importantly, let\'s celebrate our winner. It\'s Ania!', NULL, '|692|', '|692|', 'Ania Magliano wins the episode after beating Sanjeev Bhaskar in a tie-breaker.', NULL, 'taskmaster_uk_20_04_framed.png', 'taskmaster_uk_20_04_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_uk_20_04_thumb.jpg', 'Photo of a sprig of grape stems suspended from the ceiling with both grapes and olives attached to it, as well as a small red heart and a label with the number \'63\' on it (referencing the \'Find out what number Alex has written down\', \'Make a love heart with your team\', and \'Win the horse race\' tasks), with the episode title, \'Hey mate\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(838, 1, 77, 5, 1, '2025-10-09', 'Bats, bats, hang up', NULL, 1, 32, 'Alex Horne says “Bats, bats, hang up” during studio discussion of Sanjeev Bhaskar’s attempt at the ‘Do an accurate finger painting of the person on the phone’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in a possession that would most confuse a future archaeologist, pull something from one red green to another, make things genuinely awkward, do an accurate finger painting of a person on the phone, and decide whether or not to eat a lamé duck.', NULL, 'Hello, welcome! Welcome to Taskmaster, a fun entertainment show in the same way that Chairman Mao was a chilled-out wacky uncle. Let’s take a great leap forward into fun!', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And next to me, a man who thinks that men should be men, and women should be physically jacked-up enough to be able to lift those men. It’s... he likes a hench woman... little Alex Horne!', NULL, NULL, NULL, '|694|', '|694|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_uk_20_05_framed.png', 'taskmaster_uk_20_05_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_uk_20_05_thumb.jpg', 'Close-up photo of someone\'s index finger with a rainbow of paints on its tip (referencing the \'Do an accurate finger painting of the person on the phone\' task), with the episode title, \'Bats, bats, hang up\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(839, 1, 77, 6, 1, '2025-10-16', 'Is that number got curves?', NULL, 1, 692, 'Ania Magliano asks Quentin “Is that number got curves?” during the ‘Correctly guess this person’s age’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the thing Greg would most like to see Alex wearing, cut a single string to cause the greatest effect, communicate an autobiographical 10-word story to the Taskmaster, correctly wear some flippers the slowest, and guess the age of a mystery guest.', NULL, 'Welcome to Taskmaster, a group of comics battling it out to see who is the least-worst at doing a thing. No-one will learn anything from the next hour, so crack open a can and give in to the pointlessness.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And next to me, a man who told me he never struggles to get back to sleep after the alarm goes off. He simply has to listen to one of his wife\'s descriptions of a dream she had. As he put it himself, ‘They\'re so boring, I soon be snoring.’ It\'s.. little Alex Horne!', NULL, NULL, NULL, '|694|', '|694|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_uk_20_06_framed.png', 'taskmaster_uk_20_06_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_uk_20_06_thumb.jpg', 'Image of a flipper laid on the doormat of the Taskmaster house with the number 10 arranged upon it in string (referencing the \'Cut a single string to cause the greatest effect\', \'Communicate an autobiographical 10-word story to the Taskmaster\', and \'Wear the flippers correctly\' tasks), with the episode title, \'Is that number got curves?\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(840, 1, 77, 7, 1, '2025-10-23', 'Drier than you think, chalk', NULL, 1, 694, 'Phil Ellis observes “Drier than you think, chalk” during his attempt at the ‘Dribble a technicolour picture of your hero’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the best thing you can either ride or rip, steal a statue of Archimedes, dribble a technicolour picture of their hero, score exactly 63 points by bopping Alex on the head, and avoid the Taskmaster’s big golden ball.', NULL, 'Hello, there. I’m Greg Davies. Welcome to Taskmaster. They say it’s not the winning that counts, it’s the taking part, and if you’re a child watching the pre-watershed version of this show, I’m here to tell you an uncomfortable truth: you’re being told that, because you’re not good enough. That’s the kids sorted. Now... let’s see if we can break some adults.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And, next to me, a man who secretly told me – and I really must distance myself from comments like this – that he thinks that women are like electric vehicles: really good as long as they’re not in charge. It’s little Alex Horne.', NULL, 'So, what have we learnt today? Well, this is a stressful world, guys. It’s full of technology, industry and noise. It’s important to get away from it all, head to the glorious, English countryside, be at one with nature, and just let the wildlife speak to you. [a recording of Maisie’s squawk from the ‘Steal the statue of Archimedes’ task plays] But, now, let’s applaud our winner on the loo, it’s Ania Magliano.', NULL, '|692|', '|692|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_uk_20_07_framed.png', 'taskmaster_uk_20_07_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_uk_20_07_thumb.jpg', 'Image of a stuffed toy mole peering off the corner of the roof of the Taskmaster house, just above a security camera attached to the wall (referencing the \'Steal the statue of Archimedes\' and \'Get exactly 63 points by bopping Alex on the head\' tasks), with the episode title, \'Drier than you think, chalk\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(841, 1, 77, 8, 1, '2025-10-30', 'Am I an idiom?', NULL, 1, 694, 'Phil Ellis asks “Am I an idiom?” at the start of the ‘Chain charades’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the best thing that has a surprise aspect to it, answer Alex’s 10 questions, paint an animal sat on another animal from a balcony, say the most five-letter words, and play a game of chain charades.', NULL, 'Hello, I’m Greg Davies. Welcome to Taskmaster. I’d like to start on a personal note, if I may today, and tell you that Anna, the member of the crew who makes my coffees when I arrive at the studio, recently pointed out to me that in nearly 200 episodes of television, I have not once said ‘thank you’ to her. And so, I wanted to start the show by putting that right. Anna, sincerely, thank you for all your hard work. But also... your coffee tastes like crap! Clear your desk! You think I can’t replace you?! I’ve got a thousand waiting!', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And next to me, a man who tells me he’s going on holiday this year to a mysterious place where everybody spits when they talk... Wales. It’s... Little Alex Horne.', NULL, 'So, what have we learnt from today’s show? We’ve learnt this: If you want to win in life, be more Sanjeev. Care less, win more. We’ve also learnt... don’t tie your cat to a fence [audio clip of Ania Magliano’s plaintiff mew during the ‘Paint an animal sat on another animal’ task plays]. And let’s not forget this episode’s winner, Reece Shearsmith!', NULL, '|695|', '|695|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_uk_20_08_framed.png', 'taskmaster_uk_20_08_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_uk_20_08_thumb.jpg', 'Image of a red model of a moose, labelled with the word \'moose\', with a small yellow rubber duck perched on its head, in front of a blurred hedge (referencing the \'Answer Alex’s 10 questions\' and \'Paint an animal sat on another animal\' tasks), with the episode title, \'Am I an idiom?\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(842, 1, 77, 9, 1, '2025-11-06', 'A 1970s camping kettle', NULL, 1, 19, 'Greg Davies describes Ania Magliano’s scream as sounding like “a 1970s camping kettle”, during discussion of her attempt at the ‘Roll the tallest tower of bricks down the slope’ task.', 'In this episode, the contestants must bring in the most respected item that retains its credibility when they talk about it in a high-pitched voice, roll the tallest tower of bricks down the driveway, make a mannequin jockey weigh almost exactly the same as Alex, create a fantastic 15-second full-framed face film, and become the people the Taskmaster shouts at them.', NULL, 'Hi, hello, welcome to Taskmaster. I\'m Greg Davies, and I\'ve got beef. I\'ve got beef, I\'ve got lamb, I\'ve got pork and I\'ve got chicken. Who wants chicken? [he gabbles quickly like an auctioneer] Welcome to Taskmaster. Expect the unexpected, but also expect the following people…', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And next to me, a man who – according to fan fiction on the internet – I am in and out of like a sewing machine... It\'s Little Alex Horne.', NULL, NULL, NULL, '|694|', '|694|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_uk_20_09_framed.png', 'taskmaster_uk_20_09_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_uk_20_09_thumb.jpg', 'Image of a doll\'s head succulent planter, some bricks, and a jockey\'s hat on top of a wet, rusty oil drum (referencing the \'Roll the tallest tower of bricks down the slope\', \'Make your jockey weigh almost exactly the same as Alex\', and \'Make a fantastic 15-second full-framed face film\' tasks), with the episode title, \'A 1970s camping kettle\', superimposed on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(843, 1, 77, 10, 1, '2025-11-13', 'Supping from the fountain', NULL, 1, 695, 'Reece Shearsmith observes that he didn’t need to be “Supping from the fountain”, at the end of his attempt at the ‘Drink almost all the apple juice’ task.', 'In this series finale, the contestants must bring in the best tube, make exactly the same-looking drinks as their team-mate(s), drink almost all the apple juice, make water squirt out of themselves in a surprising way, and play a game of ‘Wibble bibble bam’. In a surprise series tiebreaker, several of the contestants must then guess how many ‘T’s there were in the portrait of Greg and Alex in the living room.', 'The contestants all decided to dress up as pirates for this season finale, as a \'mutiny\' against Greg\'s scoring throughout the season.', 'Hello and welcome to the Taskmaster grand final. Now, there are some that say I’m struggling to write introductions after 20 series, and to those people, I say this:<br>I’ve got a brain for business and a body for sin.<br>I give out the points to decide who will win.<br>I’m the Taskmaster, this show’s magistrate.<br>I’m inconsistent ‘cos of my swollen prostate.<br>Who dare to enter my realm of tasks?<br>Three northerners, a Gen Z, and the Sanjeev of Bhasks.<br>I’ll give them all names, I’ll give them all hope,<br>but my allegiance, as ever, remains with the Pope.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'And next to me, a man who recently confided in me, in private, that he likes women who fart. It’s... little Alex Horne!', NULL, NULL, NULL, '|693|', '|693|', NULL, NULL, 'taskmaster_uk_20_10_framed.png', 'taskmaster_uk_20_10_metatag.jpg', 'taskmaster_uk_20_10_thumb.jpg', 'Image of a red and white striped ceramic mug containing a red and white striped paper drinking straw, in front of a blurred background (referencing the \'Make exactly the same-looking drinks as your team-mate\' and \'Drink almost all the apple juice\' tasks), with the episode title, \'Supping from the fountain\', superimposed on it.', 'taskmaster_uk_20_10_2_adj.jpg', 'Image of the contestants all dressed up as pirates for the season final.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
